# Question: does a container with no grant run under the default
# confinement: only its own process in its process list, its own cgroup as
# the root, the default capabilities in its effective and bounding sets, a
# call outside the default system-call profile refused with a permission
# error, and a call number above the profile's largest answered "not
# implemented" (spec-container-1-runtime AC-7, the
# container-default-confinement test)?
#
# A unit test cannot decide it: the filter tests run the assembled program in
# the bpf package's virtual machine, and only a real kernel shows that the
# library's init loads it through Ze's seam, on every thread of the init,
# before the entrypoint runs, under the capability set the kernel applied.
#
# Method: the fixture image's run mode writes what it sees from inside to
# /report: its /proc process entries, CapEff and CapBnd from
# /proc/self/status, and the error numbers of unshare(0) and of raw call 470.
# Neither call needs a capability or changes anything, so on the host both
# succeed or fail for a reason of their own. The confined mode, run on the
# host, makes the same two calls there first: unshare(0) must succeed and
# the kernel must implement 470 (listns), so EPERM and ENOSYS in the
# container can only be the filter's answers. It prints one line per check
# and exits 1 when one fails.
#
# The capability mask is the thirteen defaults, 00000000a00425fb: CAP_MKNOD
# is withheld until the control group's device allowlist lands (phase 6 of
# the spec), and the mask is then 00000000a80425fb with the fourteenth.
#
# The store lives under /run, not in the test's work directory: in the QEMU
# guest that directory is on the 9p share of the checkout, and an overlay
# cannot take a 9p directory as its upper layer. $PORT keeps two runs apart.
option=needs-linux:caps=sys-admin
option=exclusive:group=container
option=timeout:value=60s
option=env:var=ze.test.container.store:value=/run/ze-container-test-$PORT

stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONFIG
container {
	instance confined {
	}
}
EOF_CONFIG

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-containerprobe reset /run/ze-container-test-$PORT:exit=0
cmd=background:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=config
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze-containerprobe confined /run/ze-container-test-$PORT confined:timeout=45s:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=probe: the host allows unshare(0)
expect=stdout:contains=probe: the host kernel implements call 470
expect=stdout:contains=probe: its process list holds only its own process
expect=stdout:contains=probe: its own cgroup reads as the root
expect=stdout:contains=probe: its effective capabilities are the defaults
expect=stdout:contains=probe: its bounding capabilities are the defaults
expect=stdout:contains=probe: the filter refuses unshare with a permission error
expect=stdout:contains=probe: the filter answers call 470 with not implemented
reject=stdout:contains=probe: FAIL
